(REGIONAL PLAYOUT COMPLIANCE MEMORANDUM) Tj T*
(Issued for transmission date 2029-03-01) Tj T*
(Document class: normative. This memorandum is the only) Tj T*
(place the three settlement constants below are published.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 1 - SETTLEMENT CONSTANTS) Tj T*
(separation_minimum_positions = 3) Tj T*
(billing_grain_seconds = 5) Tj T*
(regulatory_minutes_per_clock_hour = 2) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The separation minimum is counted in admitted positions) Tj T*
(inside one break. Two admitted spots that carry the same) Tj T*
(separation class must sit at least that many positions) Tj T*
(apart, so a minimum of two bars adjacent positions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The billing grain is the whole number of seconds that a) Tj T*
(delivered spot is billed in. A delivered spot is billed) Tj T*
(for the smallest whole number of grains that covers its) Tj T*
(delivered frames, and a delivery that lands exactly on a) Tj T*
(grain boundary bills that many grains and no more.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The regulatory minutage is the permitted advertising) Tj T*
(minutes inside one clock hour of the broadcast day. The) Tj T*
(cap in channel frames is the whole number of frames that) Tj T*
(those minutes occupy at the channel rate, taken toward) Tj T*
(zero. An hour whose advertising frames exceed the cap is) Tj T*
(a breach; an hour that lands exactly on the cap is not.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 2 - PERMITTED MINUTAGE BY MARKET AND CLOCK HOUR) Tj T*
(Where a market and clock hour is listed below, its permitted) Tj T*
(minutes govern that hour and replace the Section 1 figure.) Tj T*
(A market and clock hour not listed keeps the Section 1) Tj T*
(figure.) Tj T*
