(SECTION 5 - TERMS USED IN THIS MEMORANDUM) Tj T*
(admitted position: the one based index of a spot inside a break) Tj T*
(advertising frames: channel frames occupied by admitted spots) Tj T*
(avail: the commercial capacity published against one break) Tj T*
(break: a conditioned splice point inside a transmitted slot) Tj T*
(broadcast day: the day that opens at the published day start) Tj T*
(channel frame: one frame at the channel transmission rate) Tj T*
(clock hour: one whole hour measured from the broadcast day start) Tj T*
(conform: the frame exact placement of material into the day) Tj T*
(delivered frames: the frames an admitted spot actually occupies) Tj T*
(drop frame: the timecode labelling that skips frame numbers) Tj T*
(grain: the whole second unit a delivered spot is billed in) Tj T*
(junction: a point in the day where a slot start is published) Tj T*
(make good: an obligation raised against an undelivered spot) Tj T*
(market: one regional feed of the channel) Tj T*
(minor unit: the smallest indivisible unit of a currency) Tj T*
(minutage: advertising time measured inside one clock hour) Tj T*
(overrun: placement later than a fixed junction requires) Tj T*
(separation class: the competitive grouping of an advertiser) Tj T*
(slot: one scheduled transmission of one canonical asset) Tj T*
(snap: the movement of a break onto an index frame) Tj T*
(substitute: material carried in place of a blacked out slot) Tj T*
(underrun: placement earlier than a fixed junction requires) Tj T*
() Tj T*
